{"name":"Boat Anchor","hex":"#6c6b6a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boat anchor","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cumbersome, useless piece of equipment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boat_anchor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boat anchor (metaphor)","blocks":[{"text":"In amateur radio and computing, a boat anchor or boatanchor is something obsolete, useless, and cumbersome – so-called because metaphorically its only productive use is to be thrown into the water as a boat mooring. Terms such as brick, doorstop, and paperweight are similar."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat_anchor_(metaphor)"},{"title":"Anchor","blocks":[{"text":"An anchor is a device, normally made of metal, used to secure a vessel to the bed of a body of water to prevent the craft from drifting due to wind or current. The word derives from Latin ancora, which itself comes from the Greek ἄγκυρα."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Kotwica_SS_Pozna%C5%84.JPG/330px-Kotwica_SS_Pozna%C5%84.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anchor"},{"title":"Boat","blocks":[{"text":"A boat is a watercraft of a large range of types and sizes, but generally smaller than a ship, which is distinguished by its larger size or capacity, its shape, or its ability to carry boats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Motorboat_at_Kankaria_lake.JPG/330px-Motorboat_at_Kankaria_lake.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/R390A.png/500px-R390A.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/R390A.png/500px-R390A.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai